      <div type="clause" n="El. 34">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 34</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 34" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="38" ed="#liebermann"/>Þa wuduwan ⁊ þa stiopcild<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.25"/> ne sceððað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.26"/> ge, ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.27"/> hie nawer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.28"/> deriað. Gif ge þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> elles doð, hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.8"/> cleopiað to me, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.29"/> ic gehiere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.30"/> hie ⁊ ic eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.31"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> slea mid minu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> sweorde ⁊ ic gedó, þæt eowru<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.32"/> wíf beoð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.33"/> wydewan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.34"/> ⁊ eowru<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.35"/> bearn beoð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.36"/> steopcild.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.37"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 34" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="38" ed="#liebermann"/>Þa wydwan ⁊ steopcild ne sceaððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.6"/> ge hie nahwer né ne deriað. Gif ge ðonne elles doð, hie cleopiað to me, ⁊ ic gehyre hie ⁊ ic eow ðonne slea mid minu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> sweorde ⁊ ic gedó, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eowre wif beoð wydewan ⁊ eowre bearn beoð steopcild.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 34" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="39" ed="#liebermann"/>Ða wydewan ⁊ þa steopcyld ne scyþþað ⁊ ne hy nawer deriað. Gif ge þonne elles doð, hy clipiað to me, ⁊ ic gehire hy ⁊ ic eow ðonne slea mid minum sweorde and ic eow gedó, þæt eowre wif beoð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.3"/> wudewan ⁊ eowre bearn steopcyld.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 34" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="39" ed="#liebermann"/>Uiduæ et pupillo non nocebitis. Si leseritis eos, uociferabuntur ad me, et ego exaudiam clamorem eorum, et indignabitur furor meus, percutiamque uos gladio, et erunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.2"/> uxores uestræ uiduæ et filii uestri pupilli.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.3-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 34" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="254" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Þa wuduwan ⁊ þa stiopcild ne sceððað ge, ne hie nawer deriað. Gif ge þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> elles doð, hie cleopiað to me, ⁊ ic gehiere hie ⁊ ic eow þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> slea mid minu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> sweorde ⁊ ic gedó, þæt eowru wif beoð wydewan ⁊ eowru bearn beoð steopcild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="39" ed="#liebermann"/>Die Wittwen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.de.1"/> und die Waisen schädiget nicht, noch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.de.2"/> beeinträchtiget sie irgendwo. Wenn ihr jedoch anders handelt, so werden sie zu mir rufen, und ich erhöre sie und alsdann schlag ich euch mit meinem Schwerte und ich mache<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-34.lnote.de.3"/>, dass eure Weiber Wittwen werden und eure Kinder Waisen werden.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Do not harm the widows and the orphans, nor wrong them anywhere. But if you act otherwise, they will cry to me, and I will hear them, and then I will strike you with my sword and I will make your wives become widows and your children become orphans.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="255" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Widows and orphans you will not harm, nor will you ever hurt them. If you do otherwise, they will cry out to me, and I will hear them and I will then strike you with my sword; and I will arrange that your wives will be widows and your children will be orphans.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 22,22–24</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="39">Exodus 22.22; Exodus 22.23; Exodus 22.24</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[22, 22] | [22, 23] | [22, 24]</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_47">VI Atr 47</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">stepcilde <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> steopcilde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">stepcilde So; steopcilde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sceaðað <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> sceaþæþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sceaðað So; sceaþæþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hie ne hie <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> hi ne hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hie ne hie So; hi ne hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nahwer <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nahwer So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þ. hie <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þ. hie So; hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ ic g. h. <hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ ic g. h. lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gehire hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gehire hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eowe <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eowe So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ra <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ra So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wud. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> widuwan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wud. So; widuwan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eowra <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> bearn <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> eora <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eowra without bearn So; eora Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">byþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">byþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lde <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lde So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">39</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">39</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ux. ue. er. <hi rend="italic">T Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ux. ue. er. T Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">39</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ðað <hi rend="italic">verbessert von mod. Hd.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ðað corrected by a modern hand</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Witwe 1; Waise 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Witwe 1; Waise 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nene</hi> G, für ‘noch’ auch sonst</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">nene</hi> G, used for ‘nor’ elsewhere too</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-34.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘euch’ fügt zu H</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H adds ‘you’</seg></note>
